scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: game-of-thrones
run_id: 1
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Config uses from_file(path).unwrap_or_default() pattern. TEA wrote a test
    for 'missing file graceful handling' and 'malformed TOML rejection' but the malformed
    TOML test likely tests a different code path. No phase flagged that permission
    errors and parse errors are swallowed by unwrap_or_default().
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer observation #3: 'ServerError Display leaks raw server response\
    \ body (CWE-209)' \u2014 flags that the Display impl includes raw HTTP response\
    \ body that could contain stack traces and internal paths. TEA also wrote security\
    \ tests for CWE-209 error exposure, but the reviewer's finding is more directly\
    \ about the stderr leak pattern."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer observation #9: '--tenant flag accepts raw String instead of\
    \ TenantId' \u2014 explicitly flags that SiemClient uses Option<String> for tenant\
    \ instead of TenantId from axiathon-core, citing project newtype rules."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer noted toml version mismatch (observation #5) but did not flag
    that dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true. The
    Dev phase added deps with direct versions in Cargo.toml.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer observation #4: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields'\
    \ \u2014 explicitly recommends #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] to catch misconfigurations\
    \ like typos. Does not specifically mention the token-left-on-disk scenario but\
    \ catches the root cause."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)). TEA wrote config tests but this specific assertion logic flaw was not
    flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test pattern (let _ = config with
    no assert_eq! checks). TEA designed config_loading tests but did not flag this
    specific issue in existing tests.
